.page deluser 8 send a resident away from the Human Village

# SYNOPSIS
*deluser* [*--remove-home*] [*--force*] _NAME_

# DESCRIPTION
`deluser` removes the account _NAME_: its lines in `/Hakurei/etc/passwd` and `/Hakurei/etc/shadow`, its group of the same name, and its name in the member lists of the other groups. Only root may do it (try `sudo deluser`).

Accounts with a number below 1000 belong to the shrine itself and are refused unless `--force` is given. The home directory is left alone unless `--remove-home` is given; it is only removed if it lies below `/HumanVillage`.

# OPTIONS
@ *--remove-home*
    Also delete the home directory and everything in it.
@ *--force*
    Allow the removal of an account with a number below 1000.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the account does not exist, is a system account, or the caller is not root; 2 for a usage error.

# EXAMPLES
    sudo deluser alice
    sudo deluser --remove-home alice

# FILES
@ /Hakurei/etc/passwd, /Hakurei/etc/shadow, /Hakurei/etc/group
    The databases that are edited. Each is replaced in one step and, with a HUMANVILLAGE volume, kept on it as well (etckeep(8)), so the change survives a restart.

# SEE ALSO
adduser(8), passwd(5), group(5)
